        <mxCell id="5or_3En5fItqHwZpVwx8-175" parent="5or_3En5fItqHwZpVwx8-1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=#DEDEDE;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Global wiring diagram:&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;About this diagram :&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Scope : This is the &lt;u&gt;global wiring diagram&lt;/u&gt;. Shunts and switches are detailed in the &lt;u&gt;arming PCB wiring diagram&lt;/u&gt;. Wiring related to staging is detailed in the &lt;u&gt;staging wiring diagram&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Goal : The aim is to illustrate all connections and wiring in the bay. Refer to this diagram during the bay&#39;s assembly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Stage : This diagram is valid for both the booster and sustainer&#39;s avionics bays&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;About shunts and switches :&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- See Arming PCB diagram to see exact wiring and logic for shunts and switches&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- All 5 Pyrotechnic charges are disconnected and shunted by the arming PCB&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;About Wire Joints :&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Connectors: they are crimped or soldered depending on the manufacturer&#39;s recommendations&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- We buy all Molex and JST wire-to-board connectors pre-crimped. We splice the wires as needed&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- XT30 and XT60 are soldered&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Splices: wires are twisted, solder is applied to solidify, and the splice is covered with shrink tube&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="404.06" width="600" x="676.21" y="696" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
