        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="VBvmEhtEoEbFrTAlt_jw-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=#DEDEDE;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Staging wiring diagram:&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;About this diagram :&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Scope : This is the&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;staging wiring diagram&lt;/u&gt;. Avionics not related to staging are either not depicted or simplified. Refer to the global wiring diagram for details on the complete avionics bay.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Goal : The aim is to illustrate how staging charges are switched and deployed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Stage : This diagram depicts both stages&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;About Wire Joints :&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Connectors: they are crimped or soldered depending on the manufacturer&#39;s recommendations&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- We buy all Molex wire-to-board connectors pre-crimped. We splice the wires as needed&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- XT30 and XT60 are soldered&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Permanent splices: wires are twisted, solder is applied to solidify, and the splice is covered with shrink tube&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Quick splices: wires are twisted and covered with electric tape (only for splices made at launch site)&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="320" width="600" x="1010" y="35.74000000000001" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_4pWFBZjezVCJzcRwyZm-1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" value="2S1P Lion&lt;div&gt;7V4 2Ah&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
